1.Aim

To write a python program to implement various string operations.

2.Algorithm

1.Start the program.
2.Create a string variable s = "Hello Python".
3.Display the original string.
4.Find and display the length of the string.
5.Convert the string to uppercase and display it.
6.Convert the string to lowercase and display it.
7.Access and display the character at index 6.
8.Find the position of the word "Python" in the string.
9.Extract and display a substring using slicing.
10.Replace "Python" with "World" and display the result.
11.Check wheather "Python" is present in the string.
12.Concatenate another string to the original string and display it.
13.Create a string with extra spaces and remove leading and trailing spaces using strip().
14.Display the trimmed string.
15.Stop the program.

3.Source Code 

s="Hello Python"
print("Original String:",s)
print("Length:",len(s))
print("Uppercase:",s.upper())
print("Lowercase:",s.lower())
print("Character at index 6:",s[6])
print("Position of python:",s.find("Python"))
print("Slice:",s[6:])
print("Replace:",s.replace("Python","World"))
print(s)
print("Contains Python:","Python" in s)
print("Concentration:",s+" Programming")
s2="  Hello World   "
print("Trim:",s2.strip())

